      "in_summary": true,
      "summary_section": "PREAMBLE"
    },
    {
      "sentence_id": 14,
      "text": "... ... Opposite Party/s  ======================================================\n Appearance :\n For the Petitioner/s : Mr. Manoj Kumar Jha, Advocate",
      "rhetorical_role": "PREAMBLE",
      "start": 521,
      "end": 672,
      "entities": [
        {
          "text": "Manoj Kumar Jha",
          "label": "LAWYER",
          "start": 645,
          "end": 660
        }
      ],
      "in_summary": true,
      "summary_section": "PREAMBLE"
    },
    {
      "sentence_id": 15,
      "text": "For the Opposite Party/s : Mr. Pradeep Narain Kumar, APP  ======================================================\n CORAM: HONOURABLE MR. JUSTICE CHANDRA SHEKHAR JHA  ORAL ORDER 2 22-03-2023 Heard learned counsel appearing on behalf of the petitioner and learned counsel appearing on behalf of the State.\nLet the defect(s), if any, be removed within a period of four weeks from today.",
      "rhetorical_role": "PREAMBLE",
      "start": 672,
      "end": 1054,
      "entities": [
        {
          "text": "Pradeep Narain Kumar",
          "label": "LAWYER",
          "start": 703,
          "end": 723
        },
        {
          "text": "CHANDRA SHEKHAR JHA",
          "label": "JUDGE",
          "start": 816,
          "end": 835
        },
        {
          "text": "22-03-2023",
          "label": "DATE",
          "start": 850,
          "end": 860
        }
      ],
      "in_summary": true,
      "summary_section": "PREAMBLE"
    },
    {
      "sentence_id": 16,
      "text": "The petitioner seeks bail in connection with Sabaur P.S. Case No. 111 of 2022 registered for the offence under Section 363, 366, 366(A) and 376 of the Indian Penal Code (for short 'I.P.C.') and under Section 04 of the POCSO Act.\nThe accused/petitioner is named in the F.I.R. and is in custody since 17.09.2022.\nThe allegation against the petitioner is to kidnap minor daughter of the informant, aged about 17 years, for the purpose of illicit intercourse/marriage and also committed rape upon her.\nPatna High Court CR. MISC. No.74067 of 2022(2) dt.22-03-2023 Learned counsel appearing on behalf of the petitioner submitted that the petitioner implicated falsely in present case for the reason that he was in love affairs with the alleged minor daughter of the informant, which was not accepted by informant and his family members.",
      "rhetorical_role": "PREAMBLE",
      "start": 1055,
      "end": 1886,
      "entities": [
        {
          "text": "Sabaur P.S. Case No. 111 of 2022",
          "label": "CASE_NUMBER",
          "start": 1101,
          "end": 1133
        },
        {
